###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# NEP on one NVIDIA RTX 3080 (GPUMD) is stated to be about 15 times faster than GPU DeepMD and about 41 times faster than MTP (CPU, 64 Intel Xeon Platinum 8375C cores); absolute speeds are figure-only (Fig. 5).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The paper does not say explicitly that NEP was trained on the same 354 configurations as MTP; the NEP run is linked to that dataset because the paper describes one training set and 'a similar protocol'. The DeepMD model of the speed comparison is not described and not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2024constructing.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

